# TradingView Advanced Charts — how the vendored library is stored.
#
# The runtime assets (~26 MB across ~1,900 minified chunks) belong in Git LFS,
# not in plain git: committed as ordinary blobs they sit in every clone's
# history forever, including the clones of everyone who never touches the chart.
#
# **These patterns are configured and currently unused.** The push failed with
# "This repository exceeded its LFS budget", so `frontend/public/charting_library/`
# is not in this commit — see frontend/vendor/tradingview/README.md. The rules
# stay so that the moment the budget is raised, `git add` of those files does
# the right thing without anyone having to remember this.
#
# Type definitions are deliberately excluded: they are ~1.2 MB of plain text
# that TypeScript reads on every `tsc`, and an unsmudged LFS pointer would break
# compilation anywhere the filter has not run.
frontend/public/charting_library/bundles/** filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
frontend/public/charting_library/*.js filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
